---
description: testing rules for unit,integration,e2e tests
alwaysApply: false
---
**Use project folder** - use stack respective project folder like ~/backend/temp/integration/logs/ for backend stack project. ~/web/temp/e2e/logs. In the end, clear the created logs.

**Integration tests** - always run integration tests with temporary logs to read for failure tests. 

**e2e tests** - always run e2e tests with temporary logs to read for failure tests.

**fixlogs** - maintain fixlogs for fix. example: tests/performance/fixlog/, tests/integration/ tests/e2e/, tests/unit/vX.X.X. Follow semantic versioning. Format of fix logs should be breif. 
- Issue name
    - brief description
    - fix applied.

**codequality check** - run code quality checks based on yml. 
- If backend then backend*.yml
- If web then frontend*.yml
